<Docs title="Introduction">
  <h1>Introduction</h1>
  <p>
    MixRestore is a version control application designed specifically for music producers.
    It watches your DAW project files and automatically captures a snapshot every time you save,
    giving you a complete history of your project without any extra effort.
  </p>

  <h2>Why MixRestore?</h2>
  <p>
    Music production is an iterative process. You try ideas, discard them, revisit them weeks later.
    Traditional file management — saving copies like <code>track_v2_final_FINAL.als</code> — doesn't scale,
    and generic version control tools like Git aren't built for binary DAW files.
  </p>
  <p>
    MixRestore bridges that gap. It uses Git under the hood for robust version tracking, but wraps it
    in an interface designed for producers — not developers.
  </p>

  <h2>Key features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Automatic versioning</strong> — captures every save without interrupting your workflow</li>
    <li><strong>Project insights</strong> — view BPM, key, time signature, tracks, samples, and arrangement for each version</li>
    <li><strong>Instant restore</strong> — roll back to any previous version with one click</li>
    <li><strong>Version tags</strong> — label milestones like Draft, Final, Approved, Experimental</li>
    <li><strong>DAW detection</strong> — automatically detects running Ableton Live instances</li>
    <li><strong>Lightweight</strong> — runs in the background with minimal resource usage</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Supported platforms</h2>
  <p>
    MixRestore currently runs on <strong>macOS</strong> (Apple Silicon and Intel).
    Windows support is planned for a future release.
  </p>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <p>
    Ready to get started? Head to <a href="/docs/installation">Installation</a> to download and set up MixRestore,
    then follow the <a href="/docs/quick-start">Quick Start</a> guide to track your first project.
  </p>
</Docs>
